Title: Judge's X Word Puzzle No. 20
Author: Mrs. Maude Varela
Date: 1927-09-10
Byline: Submitted by Mrs. Maude Varela, Washington, D. C.
Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-09-10_93/page/n31/mode/1up
Puzzle-Number: 20
Solution-Source: https://archive.org/details/sim_judge_1927-09-17_93/page/n31/mode/1up


CROW#POPES#IMPS
RIPE#EMERY#NEAP
ACID#NITER#DATE
PENDANTS#UNITED
###ERAS#SPAR###
SADDEN#INSPECTS
ADE#STONE#SCRAP
VOID#SPEED#TUBE
ERGOT#ERROR#ELL
SENTIENT#MANTEL
###TEAS#PINE###
CARESS#SANGAREE
ALAR#ELIDE#ROVE
LOVE#LITRE#EMIR
FEEL#STEER#RELY


A1. What is always picking up after the farmer? ~ CROW
A5. Who used to hand out the Bull in the Middle Ages? (Plural.) ~ POPES
A10. What little ones have devilish ways? ~ IMPS
A14. What do people do—who do not choose to run? ~ RIPE
A15. Name a variety of corundum. ~ EMERY
A16. What is low tide at Atlantic City? ~ NEAP
A17. What sort of dispositions have reformers? ~ ACID
A18. What is used in making gun-powder? ~ NITER
A19. What is the flapper's favorite fruit? ~ DATE
A20. What do many women give ear to? ~ PENDANTS
A22. What are people who assume the Bonds of Matrimony? ~ UNITED
A24. What are always epochal? (Plural). ~ ERAS
A25. What stands "the gaff" at sea? ~ SPAR
A26. What does the first wrinkle do to a woman? ~ SADDEN
A29. What is the first thing the Prince of Wales does when he visits a new place? ~ INSPECTS
A33. Who wrote "Fables in Slang?" ~ ADE
A34. What could you call the age which is an engaging one for women? ~ STONE
A36. What often goes to the dogs? ~ SCRAP
A37. What do foreign titles often turn out to be? ~ VOID
A39. What do you need to get ahead? ~ SPEED
A41. What is one of the hollow things? ~ TUBE
A42. What horn-like fungus grows on rye? ~ ERGOT
A44. What is it always a mistake to make? ~ ERROR
A46. What did Napoleon take when given an inch? ~ ELL
A47. What kind of people have the capacity of sensation? ~ SENTIENT
A49. What is over the big fireplace in Mount Vernon? ~ MANTEL
A51. Where are reputations ruined? (Plural.) ~ TEAS
A52. What did Romeo do for Juliet? ~ PINE
A53. What will even a miserly husband give his wife? ~ CARESS
A56. What is the wine and spice drink so popular in the tropics? ~ SANGAREE
A60. What word means "wing-shaped?" ~ ALAR
A61. Give a word that means "to strike out." ~ ELIDE
A63. What do sailors like to do? ~ ROVE
A64. What will thaw even the coldest disposition? ~ LOVE
A65. What measure of capacity is a little over a quart? ~ LITRE
A66. What is a prince or chieftain of Afghanistan called? ~ EMIR
A67. How can you make a successful touch? ~ FEEL
A68. What is sometimes seen running around a cow pasture? ~ STEER
A69. What must the faithful do? ~ RELY

D1. What is the easiest game to shoot? ~ CRAP
D2. What usually betrays a newly wedded pair? ~ RICE
D3. Name a Norse God. ~ OPIN
D4. In what condition do some people leave church? ~ WEDDED
D5. What do Yankees fight for? ~ PENNANTS
D6. What does an actor do when he forgets his lines? ~ OMITS
D7. What do society wives prefer? ~ PETS
D8. How do poets write "before?" ~ ERE
D9. What do many sweet saps become? (Plural.) ~ SYRUPS
D10. What is the longest way home? ~ INDIRECT
D11. What do butchers weigh? ~ MEAT
D12. What does the average man keep under his hat? ~ PATE
D13. What has many a young man done to get a reputation for being speedy? ~ SPED
D21. Who was the Greek God of War? ~ ARES
D23. What should small children take every afternoon? (Plural.) ~ NAPS
D25. What is a mark of contempt? ~ SNEER
D26. What does a fellow do to make himself unpopular with the ladies? ~ SAVES
D27. What do love-birds do? ~ ADORE
D28. What do the queens do when they condescend to grant a favor? ~ DEIGN
D29. How do alligators appear in winter? ~ INERT
D30. In what is vinegar kept? ~ CRUET
D31. What has four legs but never walks? ~ TABLE
D32. What should X word puzzlers be able to do? ~ SPELL
D35. What does the wise man do when opportunity knocks? ~ OPENS
D38. Name an Old World migratory plover. ~ DOTTEREL
D40. What does Mrs. Henpeck do? ~ DOMINEER
D43. What are the most brilliant things about some men? ~ TIES
D45. How did our forefathers proclain Liberty? (Before the Liberty Bell got broken, of course.) ~ RANG
D48. What are often standing around artists' studios? ~ EASELS
D50. Where would you go if you wanted to get next to the girl friend? ~ NEARER
D52. What does the Spaniard call the old priest? ~ PADRE
D53. What is being exposed on Broadway? ~ CALF
D54. Name an African plant. ~ ALOE
D55. What do ill-tempered husbands do when dinner is late? ~ RAVE
D56. What must ambitious men have to build on? ~ SITE
D57. What famous city is located on the Tiber? ~ ROME
D58. What can reformers see everywhere? ~ EVIL
D59. What is that awesome feeling? ~ EERY
D62. What is the condition of a man when he's "illuminated?" ~ LIT


Misprints, kept as printed (printed → meant):
A36: What often goes to the dogs? → printed with clue number 35; 36 is meant
D45: How did our forefathers proclain Liberty? (Before the Liberty Bell got broken, of course.) → proclaim

